DESCRIPTION:Tickets $25\nPurchase Tickets\nChoreographer explores nonsense-making through fragmentation\, the compression of sound\, and movement scores for her Roulette Commission.\n\nJessica Cook shares new material developed as part of her Roulette Commission.\nThe solo\nBreaks\nby Jessica Cook is a physical exploration of nonsense-making through fragmentation\, the compression of sound\, and movement scores. The work uses improvisation scores that splice\, isolate\, reference\, and congeal macro and micro textures\, paired with constructed sound costumes and “toys” created by the artist.\nJessica Cook\nperformer & choreographer\nAdditional performers TBA\n*FREE FOR ALL ROULETTE MEMBERS *\nA livestream will be available free of charge at 8pm on the day of the performance and archived for future viewing.\nUSE CODE EARLYBIRDER AT CHECKOUT FOR $5 OFF TICKETS — ENDS AUGUST 31ST.\nJessica Cook\n(b. Kingston\, NY) has worked as a Brooklyn based choreographer for over two decades. She combines movement\, the physicality of sound making\, and sculpture in creating absurdist and strained worlds. She has presented work in venues such as La MaMa Moves Festival\, LMCC’s River to River Festival\, Pageant\, Roulette Intermedium\, Movement Research at Judson Memorial Church\, and others.\nAs a dance artist she is currently working with Tess Dworman (\nThe Con\n)\, Benjamin Akio Kimmitch (\nAllegra\n)\, visual artist Amy Beecher\, Sam Kim\, and director/dreamworker Amanda Lovejoy Street.\nShe has been an artist-in-residence at The Chocolate Factory Theater\, Movement Research\, NY Live Arts Fresh Tracks\, and MoMA PS1. She is a 2005 graduate of the SUNY Purchase Dance Conservatory and Pacific College of Health and Science.
DURATION:PT2H
LOCATION:Roulette Intermedium\, 509 Atlantic Ave\, Brooklyn\, NY
DTSTART:20261120T010000Z
SUMMARY:Breaks: A Solo Performance by Jessica Cook (Night 1)
